    "uncited": [
     "**Intersection Test:** Intersect the ray with the volume bounds or slice planes.",
     "**Parameterization:** Map $t_0$ and $t_1$ to normalized volume coordinates $[0, 1]$ to define `ray_start` and `ray_stop`.",
     "**Step Calculation:** Compute the step vector $\\vec{s} = \\text{stepLength} \\cdot \\frac{\\vec{r}}{L}$.",
     "**Transfer Function:** Map $v$ to color $C_i$ using the colormap.",
     "*   **Opacity Update:** $\\alpha'_i = \\alpha'_{i-1} + (1 - \\alpha'_{i-1}) \\alpha_{corrected}$",
     "*   **Color Update:** $C'_i = C'_{i-1} + (1 - \\alpha'_{i-1}) \\alpha_{corrected} C_i$",
     "Default calculated as $\\max(0.0001, 1 / \\text{maxSide})$.",
     "If true, alpha is modulated by volume value ($v \\cdot \\text{stepAlpha}$).",
     "If false, alpha is constant (`stepAlpha`).",
     "*   `tMin`/`tMax`: Transfer function range.",
     "Sampling rate variable ($\\nabla s$): Initialized to 0.5, allowing between two and four samplings along a ray within a cell.",
     "Pixel subdivisions: Fixed to 16^2 (256 subdivisions).",
     "Approximation of opacity: $\\alpha_i \\approx \\sigma_a(p_i, \\omega)\\Delta s$.",
     "Final form: $C = \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} [ C_i \\alpha_i \\prod_{j=0}^{i-1} t_j ]$.",
     "Runs at 1/8 resolution, launching one ray per 8×8 pixel block.",
     "Each ray walks the world at tile granularity and writes the first-hit distance to an `r32float` texture.",
     "*   **Time Complexity:** $O(P \\cdot N)$, where $P$ is the number of pixels and $N$ is the number of samples per ray.",
     "Early ray termination can significantly reduce $N$ for opaque regions.",
     "*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(V)$ for the volume texture, where $V$ is the number of voxels."
    ]
   }
  }
